      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(music): stop hanging when generated asset downloads drip forever",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where music generation providers (e.g. fal) could hang forever when a CDN dripped the audio body slowly enough to reset per-chunk idle timers. `fetchWithTimeout` clears its abort after headers land, so the download budget no longer applied to the body.\n\nAdditionally restores transient HTTP retry that was lost when the non-2xx validation was placed outside `executeProviderOperationWithRetry`. A 503 from the CDN should trigger a retry before failing the download.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTwo changes in `downloadGeneratedMusicAsset`:\n\n1. **Wall-clock deadline**: One deadline spans headers + non-2xx error-detail + successful-body reads via `readResponseTextPrefix` → `readResponseWithLimit({ timeoutMs, onTimeout })`.\n\n2. **Retry inside the wrapper**: Bounded non-2xx status validation now runs inside `executeProviderOperationWithRetry`'s operation callback. When the CDN returns HTTP 503, the error is thrown inside the retry loop so `isTransientProviderOperationError` (which matches `/\\bHTTP\\s*(?:500|502|503|504)\\b/i` in the error message) can retry it. Previously the non-2xx check ran after the retry wrapper returned, so transient statuses were never retried.\n\nNon-overlapping: #108982 bounds video-generation downloads; #109076 bounds Discord webhook bodies.\n\nCollision check: no open hang-class PR on `downloadGeneratedMusicAsset` / `src/music-generation/provider-assets.ts`.\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Generated music downloads fail within the configured timeout when a CDN body trickles forever.\n- Transient CDN errors (503, etc.) are retried once before surfacing the failure.\n- Music generation no longer sticks forever on a slow-drip CDN response.\n\n## Evidence\n\nExact head: `47751f5bb25ddf2f054f5c2beeb4417f727a4b56`\n\n`oxfmt --check src/music-generation/provider-assets.ts src/music-generation/provider-assets.test.ts` — passed.\n`git diff --check` — clean.\n\n### Tests\n\n```bash\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/music-generation/provider-assets.test.ts -- --run --reporter=verbose\n```\n\n```\n ✓ bounds a dripping download body with one wall-clock deadline 282ms\n ✓ throws on non-2xx HTTP status without retry 16ms\n ✓ retries on transient HTTP status before succeeding 263ms\n ✓ does not bound a dripping body when only chunk idle timeout is used 406ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  4 passed (4)\n```\n\n- **Drip body (200)**: continuous drip with `timeoutMs: 250` rejects with timeout error, wall-clock deadline covers body.\n- **Non-2xx (400)**: immediate 400 response throws HTTP status error without retry (400 is explicitly non-retryable).\n- **Retry (503 → 200)**: first request returns 503, retry wrapper detects transient error via `/\\bHTTP\\s*503\\b/i`, second request succeeds. Proves `requestCount === 2`.\n- **Negative control**: idle-only `chunkTimeoutMs: 100` on a 20ms drip stays unsettled past 400ms — proves old code path has no wall-clock bound.\n\n### Mutation check\n\n```bash\n# Temporarily revert the fix (stash provider-assets.ts)\ngit stash -- src/music-generation/provider-assets.ts\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/music-generation/provider-assets.test.ts -- --run -t \"retries on transient\"\n# → FAIL: \"test music download failed (HTTP 503): Service Unavailable\"\n#    (503 not retried — thrown outside retry wrapper)\ngit stash pop\n# Restore → test passes (503 retried → 200 success)\n```\n\n### Not tested\n\nLive fal CDN against real provider endpoints — requires real API credentials.",
